  "implemented": [
    "Schema55 preserves an inactive owned reaction until the following actor-prefix recovery, separately from ordered outgoing sequence layers that can continue to fade after action recovery.",
    "C++ and Python codecs preserve sequence timing, retirement duration/optional absolute anchor, signed zero and outgoing order. Legacy promotion adds no reaction, fade timer or outgoing layer. Anchored outgoing retirement requires initialized timing.",
    "Contact preparation accepts an explicitly supplied outgoing strike only when its cause, group, displayed time and existing native timing match the replaced strike. Publication shares the existing atomic resources/action/RNG transaction.",
    "Prepared reaction frames stage actor-clock advancement, strict Start/inclusive End checks, native manager timing and retirement. Positive retirement anchors on the manager update and becomes inactive at its stored end; nonpositive retirement deactivates immediately. Outgoing expiry removes only the detached layer.",
    "Commit rejects stale actor/life/melee/clock/action ownership and publishes without callbacks, allocation or RNG consumption. Prefix recovery releases the owned action, retaining BlockHit action6 only with an actual BlockIdle supplied by the caller."
  ],
